fix(install): let launchd spawn jobs from /usr/libexec

launchd has no direct job spawn.  Every LaunchDaemon job is started as
posix_spawnp("/usr/libexec/xpcproxy", {"xpcproxy", <service>, ...}) at
0x100024abc; the only other spawn sites are the boot-task direct run and
launchd's own re-exec.  The installer's prefix table had no /usr/libexec
entry and the current root volume does not carry the binary, so a job
would fail with ENOENT even when launchd itself starts.

Add /usr/libexec/ to both copies of the allowlist (bsd/dev/kebab_install.c
and scripts/make-minimal-userland.py), and add the real xpcproxy as the
sixth base.kist entry.  The binary is 96,352 bytes; its three dylib
dependencies are all in the split shared cache and its cdhash is in
Apple's 2,760-entry static trust cache.

The earlier note said the binary is in Cryptex1,SystemOS.  It is not: the
cryptex's /usr has only lib/, and /usr/libexec does not exist in that
volume.  /usr/libexec/xpcproxy is in the OS root DMG (mtree inode
1152921500312217273); docs/IOS-USERLAND.md now records the correction and
the extraction command.

The new base.kist is 6 entries / 1,716,034 bytes installed / 655,360
bytes on the wire (640.0 KiB, 10 chunks), SHA-256
eec6cbefbb52a671275fef924f088c5ffded10dbeda829438d98e53bb28aa5dc.
It was packed and re-read with pack-userland.py --verify.  The bring-up
orchestrator and the fake-board fixture now expect six base entries.

